<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Stability pact deal possible tonight-Jelved.</title>
<headline>Stability pact deal possible tonight-Jelved.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish economy minister Marianne Jelved said on Thursday there was a chance that EU finance ministers could agree a deal tonight on a stability pact to protect the value of the planned single currency.</p>
<p>'It should be a possibility to finish the negotiations tonight,' she told reporters, speaking in English.</p>
<p>Jelved, attending a special session of finance ministers in Dublin ahead of a two-day EU summit, said there were only a few issues left to resolve.</p>
</text>
